### General Project Context (MkDocs Blog)

- This is a personal blog built with the static site generator [MkDocs](https://www.mkdocs.org/) and the [Material for MkDocs](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/) theme.
- The main configuration is in `mkdocs.yml`.
- All content is located in the `docs/` directory as Markdown files.
- Custom theme overrides are in the `overrides/` directory.
- All automation (building, image optimization, stats, testing) is bundled in `site_manager.py` in the project root.

### Local Development Commands

- **To build the site:** Run `python site_manager.py build`. This also optimizes images and generates stats.
- **To serve the site locally:** Run `python site_manager.py serve`. The site will be available at `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.
- **To do a quick build without optimization:** Run `python site_manager.py build --no-optimize`.
- **To test the built site:** Run `python site_manager.py test`; validate media paths with `python site_manager.py check`.